<title>HUNGARY: Central Europe's CESI advances on Polish gains.</title>
<headline>Central Europe's CESI advances on Polish gains.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index advanced on Tuesday to end at 1,533.08 points, up 2.85 points or 0.19 percent, the Budapest Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The index rose mainly due to gains of Polish shares.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses. -- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
